          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "பிசகு — picaku — \"to be dislocated; to go wrong\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "விழுந்ததில் அவருடைய தோள் பிசகியது. viḻuntatil avaruṭaiya tōḷ picakiyatu. His shoulder was dislocated in the fall."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past (it …): பிசகியது, picakiyatu."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Said of the joint, so the past is பிசகியது. Of plans too: கணக்கு பிசகியது, the sums went wrong."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "பிசகு (picaku) is native Dravidian (DEDR 4131), from a false step to a slipped joint."
            }
          ]
        },
